      "full_clause_reason": "The actual real pairing has symmetry, both additivities and scalar linearities, strict self-positivity and sqrt length. EuclideanSpace pairing is explicitly the source finite dot sum; its l2 length is the sqrt sum of squares. A real symmetric positive-definite matrix supplies all five weighted bilinear identities, strict positivity, sqrt length and zero iff. Positive diagonal entries supply actual positive definiteness and exact weighted sum. The exact source definition and examples are covered without asserting that the ordinary Pi sup norm is the Euclidean norm."
